  "description": "BTPS 1.1 item J, host identity lookup repaired (fix list 1), and fix-list item 9 (padded keys in DNS). parse: each TXT record, as the strings a resolver returns, read into its tags; a value keeps every '=' after the first. dns: the address's own identity record, looked up first over a fake zone in which every other name has no record (ENOTFOUND): a key, absent (the client then asks the host), or an error. lookup: answers a host sends to `request`, checked with the zone's keys: accepted with the key record, or refused with the error code. The server-side defects (the double hash, the response schema, the socket) are behaviour, tested over real TLS in src/server/test/identityLookup.integration.test.ts.",
